# Description-based routing golden set — adversarially-confusable single-skill picks.
# Each task shares surface keywords with the `distractor` (the tempting wrong sibling
# that carries a "Not for … — use …" cross-ref) but the correct pick is `expect`.
# Metric of interest: does the cross-ref reduce distractor-picks? See run-desc-routing.py.
#
# CORRECTION 2026-09-11 — q7_pod_hardening: expect was `sota-kubernetes`, which is wrong by
# TWO independent standards inside this library, neither of them a model score: the router's
# rule 9 ("pod/container/workload isolation mechanics -> sota-sandboxing") and
# sota-kubernetes' OWN description ("NOT pod-level securityContext/seccomp (sota-sandboxing)").
# The task is literally securityContext/runAsNonRoot/capabilities on pods. expect is now
# sota-sandboxing and sota-kubernetes becomes the distractor, which is what the case was
# always testing. Found while running the ROADMAP 53 keyword ablation, where this was the
# ONLY case that moved — so note the provenance honestly: the defect surfaced from a result,
# and the justification for fixing it is the two standards above, not the result.
# Consequence for the published §5 xref number: the DELTA is unaffected (both arms carried
# the same label), but the absolute correct-rate it reported as 0.80 was understated.
#
# SELECTION RULE — adversarially-confusable tasks: each names the correct skill and the tempting wrong sibling that shares surface keywords. Chosen by confusability, never by a model's score.
# MEASUREMENT set — a lift may be reported from it, so cases must never be selected by a model's score (`sota-llm-engineering` rules/01 §8).
